From 2e487d7cd44d8497588ab35821ea3c6b68406e20 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: wray-lee <wray-lee@outlook.com>
Date: Sat, 17 Oct 2026 00:32:05 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] fix(stop): abort in-flight provider streams and backpressure
 chunk publishing

`/stop` now raises an interrupt flag the blocking provider request observes, so
every route (reliable, codex, gemini, sse/curl) aborts its in-flight stream
promptly instead of finishing the turn. Stream-chunk publishing is bounded:
a full outbound queue returns Timeout instead of parking the turn, and a stopped
turn's queued chunks are dropped and its stop marker cleared. Slack streamed
deltas are throttled to the presenter's one-flush-per-interval minimum.
